      <p class="text-theme-primary text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> The two welded wire mesh panel sizes you will see quoted by almost every <a href="/wire-mesh-hebei/" class="text-theme-primary underline">Hebei factory</a> are <strong>2.0 × 2.0 m</strong> (European standard format) and <strong>2.4 × 1.2 m</strong> (UK/imperial format). Rolls are typically 1.0–2.5 m wide × 25–50 m long. Because Anping factories serve both metric and imperial markets, they routinely cut "standard" panels to 8 ft × 4 ft, 6 ft × 3 ft, and other imperial sizes—custom dimensions are normal, not a premium service. What you must specify is not just length × width but also wire diameter with tolerance, aperture, edge finish (plain vs bent edge), and the dimensional tolerance (±5 mm length/width is standard). Check the resulting weight with the <a href="/tools/welded-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-primary underline">welded mesh weight calculator</a> before accepting any quote.
      </p>
    </div>

