        Ask five suppliers for "standard welded wire mesh panels" and you may receive five different answers—because "standard" means whatever the factory's main export market historically demanded. This is actually good news for buyers: Anping's <a href="/anping-wire-mesh/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">wire mesh cluster</a> produces metric and imperial formats side by side on the same lines, so getting your exact size usually costs nothing extra. The risk is ambiguity. This article lists the sizes that actually exist on Hebei production lines, the tolerances factories work to, and the exact wording to put in your inquiry so a 2.4 × 1.2 m panel doesn't arrive as 2.35 × 1.18 m without recourse.
      </p>
