          <li>☐ Panel size: 2440 × 1220 mm exact, ±5 mm, squareness ≤3 mm diagonal</li>
          <li>☐ Aperture: 50 × 50 mm nominal, ±3%</li>
          <li>☐ Wire diameter: 4.0 mm ±5% (specify bare wire, before coating, if galvanized)</li>
          <li>☐ Edge: bent V-fold 25 mm on all four sides (or plain edge, or selvage)</li>
          <li>☐ Zinc coating: ≥275 g/m², ASTM A90 test method</li>
          <li>☐ Standard: ASTM A974 / ISO 9044 as applicable</li>
          <li>☐ Quantity, packaging (bundles of 10 on steel pallet, banded + wrapped), labeling</li>
          <li>☐ Incoterm and port (e.g., FOB Xingang), and whether dimensions are metric or imperial-exact</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-4">
        Before sending, run the theoretical weight through the <a href="/tools/welded-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">weight calculator</a>. A factory quoting well below that weight is quoting thinner wire or lighter zinc—catch it at RFQ stage, not at the port.
      </p>
